---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ScienceGoals from "../components/ScienceGoals.astro";
import GalaxyGallery from "../components/GalaxyGallery.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="MISTY"
  description="Mapping the ISM and Stellar populations of TinY galaxies"
>
  <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
    <h1 id="intro-heading" class="visually-hidden">About MISTY</h1>
    <div class="intro__prose">
      <p class="intro__lead">
        How do galaxies turn gas into stars, regulate their growth, and assemble
        their mass across cosmic time? At the heart of this question is the
        baryon cycle, the continual exchange of matter and energy between stars,
        the interstellar medium (ISM), and the large-scale circumgalactic environment. 
        Gas cools into molecular clouds that collapse to form stars, while massive
        stars return energy and newly synthesized elements through radiation,
        winds, and supernovae, disrupting their natal clouds and recycling
        material within galaxies and into their surroundings.
      </p>
      <p>
        MISTY maps key stages of this cycle in the low-mass, low-metallicity
        regime: a largely unexplored environment that encompasses the majority
        of star-forming conditions in the Universe by number. We are building a
        multi-wavelength, high-resolution view of nearby dwarf galaxies,
        combining observations from the ground and space to resolve the stars, 
        gas, and dust that drive galaxy evolution on 10-100 pc scales. 
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ScienceGoals />

  <GalaxyGallery />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    max-width: var(--reading-max);
  }

  .intro__prose {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .intro__lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .intro__prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1.2em;
  }

  .intro__prose p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .intro__prose {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .intro__lead {
      font-size: 1.1875rem;
      line-height: 1.72;
    }
  }
</style>
